       }
      ],
      "text": "Rasagiline:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 1 mg once daily as monotherapy; with levodopa start 0.5 mg once daily, increasing to 1 mg if needed. With ciprofloxacin or other CYP1A2 inhibitors, don't exceed 0.5 mg once daily. Selegiline: 10 mg/day as 5 mg at breakfast and 5 mg at lunch."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Advise patients not to exceed selegiline 10 mg/day and explain the 'cheese reaction'; rare hypertensive reactions with tyramine-containing foods have occurred even at the recommended dose, and selectivity for MAO-B falls as the dose rises."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
